\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Three representations of the V-logic \(L_{12}\). (a) Greechie-style hypergraph. (b) Atom-state incidence schema, with colored cells indicating \(v_i(x)=1\) and gray cells indicating \(v_i(x)=0\). (c) The grammar-oriented tile realization, the \emph  {Quantum Square}. In each row, squares left of the black separator correspond to states in which the atom is true; squares right of the separator correspond to states in which it is false. Blank cells are layout padding only.}}{5}{figure.1}\protected@file@percent }
